 "govtech": {
  "round": "take-home",
  "tag": "inspired",
  "source": "GovTech take-home: Teacher Admin API (OneCV), commonstudents",
  "evidence": "Public GitHub repos of the GovTech Teacher Admin API / OneCV take-home define a commonstudents endpoint returning students common to all the given teachers; this is its core logic as a pure function.",
  "extensions": [
   "Write it in SQL: <code>SELECT student FROM registrations WHERE teacher IN (...) GROUP BY student HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT teacher) = n</code>, where <code>n</code> is the number of <b>distinct</b> teachers asked for. Why <code>DISTINCT</code>, and what goes wrong if a registration row is duplicated without it?",
   "Expose it as <code>GET /api/commonstudents?teacher=a%40x.com&amp;teacher=b%40x.com</code>. How do you read a repeated query parameter, and what status do you return when no teacher is given?",
   "Which index makes the SQL fast? A composite unique index on <code>(teacher, student)</code> also stops duplicate registrations at write time.",
   "Return students common to <b>at least k</b> of the teachers instead of all of them. With a <code>Counter</code> over the requested sets this is one more line."
  ]
 }
